        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a for-profit public company headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana, and trades under the ticker LUMN. Its website describes the company as a provider of a global fiber network, secure networking, edge cloud, and AI-ready infrastructure, and calls it the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy.\n\nThe company's site presents customer examples involving AI-related networking. It says built-in automation replaced Arctic Glacier's manual operations, that the New York Yankees use diverse 100G paths and automatic failover for real-time scalability, and that American Family Care received a private, low-latency network designed for heavy AI workloads. The site also states that Prometheus Hyperscale anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady, and that Lumen's retail network provides security for transactions and protection from DDoS attacks.\n\nThe company's legal exposure includes 57 matters in Louisiana.",
